<resources>
    <!--
      The brand, for the frame Android draws BEFORE JavaScript exists.

      Without this the launcher shows a white sheet for the second or so it
      takes to start the runtime, and the app appears to flash before it opens.
      The colour is duplicated here because a native resource cannot read
      `@cartze/core/theme` — see `src/common/brand.ts` for the rest of what a
      rename has to touch.

      THE SHOPPING SIDE'S OCEAN. This app wears the same Meadow palette as the
      customer app (`ThemeProvider`'s default), so this is `meadowThemes.light
      .primary` and the first frame hands over to a screen of the same colour.
    -->
    <color name="brand">#1A759F</color>
    <!--
      THE LAUNCHER ICON'S GROUND — the LOGO's teal, not the app's primary.

      Supplied artwork: a rounded square with its own deep teal ground and the
      T mark on it. Same family as the splash above, eight degrees apart on
      the hue wheel, so tapping the icon still leads somewhere that looks
      related — which is the only thing this rule was ever about.
    -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#0B4A50</color>
</resources>
